en:
I was so sure it was Sanae lying there that it gave me a real shock.
I was so embarrassed my face was on fire.
Right after that, the school nurse came back.{p}

Clink, clunk... like that.
There was no class in the chemistry lab that period.
So I wondered what it was and peeked in, and...{p}

Just then,
"{f:Whoa|Eek}!"
With a pathetic yelp, {f:I|I} landed on my backside on the floor.{p}

"Are you okay,
{c}{f:|}?"
Fukuzawa asked, but she couldn't hold back her laughter.
And not only her{f:.|.}
Everyone was laughing at me without holding back.
{f:But|But} right then, there was something on {f:my|my} mind more than everyone's laughter...{p}

"Ah, there it is!"
That's right. From under the chair {f:I|I}'d been sitting on, what looked like that ritual paper had turned up{f:.|.}
It {f:looked like|looked like} nothing but a scrap of paper, but...
Could what just happened have been this paper's doing{f:?|?}
Now that I thought about it, it was like the chair had thrown me off...
Still laughing, Fukuzawa picked up the scrap of paper and tucked it into her skirt pocket.{p}

Something seemed off, but...
if Sanae was fine with it, I figured, well, okay.
I treated my jammed finger and went back to P.E.{p}

The classroom was empty and hollow, and it seemed like no one was there.
I couldn't sense anyone at all.
But Sanae was there, in that classroom.{p}

The weather was nice, so maybe the roof?
Ah, just as I thought.
Sanae was on the roof.{p}

Sanae smiled at the Reaper like an old friend, took something round and squishy out of her skirt pocket, and said,
"Ketsu's soul, right here..."
That's definitely what she said.{p}

I picked up the receiver and dialed, checking each number one by one.
And then, just as I put my finger on the last digit...!
On the TV screen were words I couldn't believe...{p}

The light faded right away.
After it was gone, it seemed like nothing was there.
But that wasn't true.{p}

"I see..."
Fukuzawa looked a little worried.
If what she said is true, then that is {f:one incredibly|one really} cursed scrap of paper{f:.|, isn't it?}
{f:No way|No way} would I go out of my way to hunt it down just to see it{f:.|.}
That girl Sanae apparently said,
"The bed talked to me,"
but there's no guarantee at all that it's true{f:.|, after all.}
The 'blood ritual' might be a spell that lets something in this school, say, an evil spirit, possess objects and make them move.
If so, then the paper vanishing starts to seem meaningful, too{f:.|.}
Maybe it no longer needs to exist here.
Or maybe it has gone off to someone else who wants it.{p}

"You're right. Now I don't have to get rid of it.
I should think of it as a good thing."
{f:Yes|Yeah}, {f:I'll|I'll} just call it a good thing.
So that rustle I heard in my pocket just now must all be in my head{f:.|.}
"Okay, that's the end of my story.
Next is... whose turn?"{p}
